From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <subscribe@johnericson.me>
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] uts/idmap: find the rpcgen-generated `idmap_prot.h`

`idmap_xdr.c` is generated by `rpcgen` from `uts/common/rpcsvc/idmap_prot.x`
into `uts/common/idmap`, and it opens with a bare

    #include "idmap_prot.h"

Sun `rpcgen` writes the path it was given, so on a stock build that line
carries the full `$(SRC)/uts/common/rpcsvc/` prefix and resolves. Other
`rpcgen` implementations emit only the basename, and then nothing on the
compile line names the directory the header actually lives in -- the module
compiles `../../common/idmap/idmap_xdr.c`, so the quoted-include search
starts in `uts/common/idmap`, and `-Y I,../../common` only covers
`<rpcsvc/...>` spellings:

    ../../common/idmap/idmap_xdr.c:6:10: fatal error: idmap_prot.h: No such file or directory

Name the directory explicitly rather than depending on which `rpcgen` ran.
---
 usr/src/uts/intel/idmap/Makefile | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/usr/src/uts/intel/idmap/Makefile b/usr/src/uts/intel/idmap/Makefile
index c730edbba0..b843f58d65 100644
--- a/usr/src/uts/intel/idmap/Makefile
+++ b/usr/src/uts/intel/idmap/Makefile
@@ -51,6 +51,15 @@ include $(UTSBASE)/intel/Makefile.intel
 #
 LDFLAGS += -Nsys/doorfs -Nstrmod/rpcmod
 
+#
+#	idmap_xdr.c is generated by rpcgen from uts/common/rpcsvc/idmap_prot.x,
+#	and rpcgen emits a bare `#include "idmap_prot.h"` -- the basename of its
+#	input, with no directory. The header is generated next to the .x file,
+#	not next to the .c, so a quoted include cannot find it from
+#	uts/common/idmap. Name the directory it does live in.
+#
+INC_PATH	+= -I$(UTSBASE)/common/rpcsvc
+
 # Function variables unused for rpcgen-generated code
 # Constant conditions for do { } while (0) macros
 #
-- 
2.51.0

